[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue. The reports in it show three problems, and
each has its own ticket with the number of reports it covers. Engineering closed #4471 on
5 October: the parser is fixed and the booking-v3 form is retired. The one-day move is still open.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is closed, but not every report in it is solved. The one-day move has no fix and no
decision. Do not tell a reporter with a one-day move that #4471 fixed it.
</Callout>

## What the reports show

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

- **`parser`**: the tenant writes the day first and the shared parser read the month first.
  7 April went out as 4 July. Every tenant in #4471, every channel. Fixed by
  `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
- **`hint`**: only on booking-v3 tenants, only through the form. The form told people to type
  `MM/DD/YYYY` and then read what they typed day first. Same symptom, different code. Won't
  fix: the form is retired, so the hint is gone with it.
- **`one-day`**: the date is right, the day is not. "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
  Toronto got Monday." "Only June." No day/month pair in these reports swaps, so neither change
  above touches them. The desk noted them in `desk-notes.json`; the #4471 page files them under
  `parser` by tenant, as a footnote. The last one says the reporter stopped reporting these, so
  this count is a floor.

## How they were told apart

- One id, one report: the export pages overlap, so ids are counted once.
- The cause follows the tenant (`causes.ts`), not intake's tag. Intake guesses from the
  reporter's browser and disagrees with the tenant often.
- The subject line says nothing about the cause. Subjects repeat across all three problems, so
  [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merged them into one ticket.

## For the desk

- A new report about a one-day move goes to the one-day ticket, not to #4471. Ask the reporter
  where each attendee is: the reports point at time zones.
- Decision 0001 is accepted and stays as written. Merging on subject alone is what hid these
  problems; it needs a new decision record.

